+# Author proposal status, 2026-09-16
+
+All three final notes have current surface status `conditional-support` and proposed target type `bounded_theorem`. The lattice graph, Clifford representation, Wilson operator, paired matter, coupling, mass, time step, clock calibration and endpoint state are supplied. None is an empirical prediction or an axiom-derived selection.
+
+| Proposal | Proposed result | Dependencies and remaining obligation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Block02 | Exact temporal runs and local physical-curl derivative bounds independent of time spacing, spatial volume and duration, for m>3kappa on open slabs | The supplied massive determinant and an explicitly chosen integer filling; no gauge phase follows |
+| Block03 | Exact positive Fock boundary realization and its normalized finite-graph continuous-time Hamiltonian | Classical Wilson transfer/minor machinery, derived prefactors; no thermal trace or arbitrary fermion insertions |
+| Block04 | Actual calibrated gauge-matter transfer, exact open determinant weight, and fixed-graph joint regulator/state limits | Current Block03 and provisional PR8162 at0f02dc5127416f347e231bbd8aa7c2a8b58a02fa; no spatial thermodynamic exchange |
+
+The six primary finite programs and formula mutations are all personal checks. Distinct calculation paths test several load-bearing identities; none is an independent audit. Preserved failures and the initially equivalent orientation mutation are documented in review/NUMERICAL_HISTORY.md. No retained promotion or formal audit verdict is authored.
+
+The heavy-mass derivative bound is genuinely volume uniform within its stated model, whereas the transfer/state convergence proof is only for a fixed graph. Those are different statements. Neither proves a gapless interacting phase or the limit of the physical ground state as spatial volume grows. The absence of that proof here does not contradict any framework axiom.
+
+Formal registration, restricted audit mapping, helper allowlisting if applicable, canonical runner evidence, integrated landing pipeline and independent ratification remain pending before retained landing. This is a reviewable discovery checkpoint. No axioms, primitives, editable prompts, governance files or main science surfaces were changed.
