+# Personal proof review
+
+This is an author review, not an independent review or audit. The main base is e0ef7cf4633034a8c1e6d57f5812cc4275bf1349. The standing instruction revision is068e916ca37b004757ad3a3c082857a91dc37215 on ai/execution. Both were fetched and unchanged at the final source refresh. A mistaken fetch of nonexistent ai/planning failed; it did not change science or supply a planning receipt. The actual standing branch was then fetched explicitly.
+
+## Temporal expansion and source geometry
+
+The inverse contains two temporal spin projections, including their sum at run length0. Its norm bound alone does not prove locality. The absolute word estimate separately uses the rank2 spin trace, its factor2^(-ell), all2^ell temporal signs, and the closing time equation fixing one run length. Losing that constraint loses the factor delta per root. The weighted temporal geometric series is valid under delta<=1/mu and mu_b>6kappa. Summing root coefficients converts that factor into the physical time measure.
+
+The local integer filling is an interval chain homotopy followed by coordinate contractions inside the visited coordinate box. Its temporal area is bounded in physical time units; t_j is now explicitly defined as physical time in the final note. Translation counting and Young/Holder give the physical Lp derivative estimate, including the delta^-1 counting-measure conversion. The entrywise Hessian envelope retains the same factor. Conversion to counting variables Omega=sqrt(delta)F leaves a delta^-1/2 factor in the third derivative; it is explicitly stated, not silently bounded away.
+
+The final rectangle sum includes time index0; an original lower-limit typo was corrected to agree with the already-correct finite program. Odd spatial walks cannot close on this free bipartite box. The sharper heavy-mass estimate treats the two-hop temporal rectangle separately; spatial loops of length4 still contribute to its O(mu^-3) third-derivative bound. The constants are sufficient and very loose, not optimized practical mass thresholds.
+
+## Boundary model and dynamical gauge join
+
+The Schur determinant prefactor is proved by elimination and its two cancelling permutation signs, not by matching zeros. The recurrence X has a plus-sign first derivative. The physical minus-sign evolution follows from inverse complementary minors and the adjoint relation between reversed and chronological products. No commuting-slice assumption is made. The gauge-dependent finite-step scalar is retained; the continuum energy shift follows from its first derivative.
+
+The canonical boundary state fills the negative gamma0 modes, with a conjugate partner making the local charge neutral. This is one supplied realization of the determinant, not a derived flavor law. Generic Wilson transfer, canonical minors and anisotropic block reduction are classical or directly present in the cited literature. The campaign does not claim their invention.
+
+The dynamical transfer is a positive sandwich of the exact paired square root and the actual calibrated gauge kernel. Its boundary vectors each carry an additional half-factor, yielding a full matter/spatial multiplier at every slice. The Markov matrix already contains transition probabilities; only one outer normalized counting measure remains in the finite path sum. The one-edge direct sum checks this normalization and the local Gauss reduction.
+
+A declared graph-dependent scalar shift makes the exact transfer contractive. Its first derivative is finite Laurent even though the exact square root has infinite Fourier support. This is sufficient for the common core argument. The imported PR8162 proof hypotheses are enumerated and checked; its source revision is frozen. The all-mode kinetic floor and positivity identity then control fixed-graph state limits. No heat-trace bound uniform in graph size is claimed. The open boundary amplitude need not select the global ground state without additional sector/overlap results.
+
+## Verification limits and disposition
+
+Six finite programs challenge separate algebraic constructions. The physical-curl Hessian program at fixed slice count has shrinking physical duration as delta shrinks; it is not cited as a fixed-duration limit. A separate third-variation program keeps duration0.3 while increasing slices. The coupled transfer test uses a one-edge graph, no magnetic plaquette, and an invariant1296-dimensional Fock sector; it does not numerically test a photon or the full many-body thermal space. The arbitrary-vector generator comparison prevents the open boundary amplitude alone from masking an incorrect electric energy.
+
+The final checks and final mutation outcomes support offering these proposals for independent review. They do not establish correctness of every general estimate. The intended disposition is a draft discovery PR with no retained landing, audit verdict, axiom update or main merge. The campaign continues personally after this milestone.
